Description: Ambient light: two modes (adjust around the slider, or a fixed curve)
 New keys in org.gnome.settings-daemon.plugins.power:
  ambient-mode 'adjust' (default): room light moves the brightness up to
   ambient-adjust-range (default 25) percent above or below the slider; the
   full range is reached at 8x brighter or darker than when the slider was
   last moved, and moving the slider makes the current light the reference.
  ambient-mode 'curve': a fixed lux -> brightness curve (log scale); the
   slider shifts it, and in the middle the curve applies as is.
 gnome-shell applies target + slider - 50 %, so both modes only change the
 target gnome-settings-daemon sends. Stock GNOME instead renormalises to
 two thirds of full scale at the reference light, with no limit.
Author: SB4-Edge-Linux
Forwarded: not-needed
